  "markdown_content": "## Environmental Crisis at Sacred Yamuna River\\n\\nThe Yamuna River, one of India's most sacred waterways, has become a critical environmental concern as vast sections of its surface in New Delhi are now covered with toxic white foam. The alarming pollution levels are primarily attributed to industrial pollutants being discharged into the river from factories surrounding the capital city.\\n\\n## Health Impacts\\n\\nEnvironmental experts warn that the contamination poses severe health risks to the millions of residents living along the river's banks. The toxic foam, which contains high levels of ammonia and phosphates, has been linked to:\\n\\n* Respiratory problems\\n* Skin conditions among local communities\\n\\n## Government Response\\n\\nLocal authorities have faced mounting pressure to address the crisis, as the river's condition continues to deteriorate despite previous cleanup efforts. The situation is particularly distressing given the Yamuna's religious and cultural significance to the Indian population.",
